BEGIN_DESC
AtmoFX volumetric deck: needs the AtmoFX fork of D3D9Client (_src\build_d3d9\install_client.bat; "install_client.bat stock" restores the stock client). One ammonia cloud deck 425-480 km above Jupiter's reference radius is ray-marched in 3D: chromophore-tinted (ochre, cream, brown) clouds on a flow map of bands and vortices (Config\AtmoFX_Volume.cfg: sizes, density, steps), moved by zonal jets. Beyond 1500 km the stock layer shows.
The probe descends from 1500 km to 470 km at 8 km/s (real time, ~2 min), drifting north at 0.3 km/s. Numpad8/2 climb/descend (stops the descent, Shift x10), Numpad4/6/5 drift. Ctrl+arrows / right mouse - look around.
END_DESC

BEGIN_ENVIRONMENT
  System Sol
  Date MJD 60970.5
END_ENVIRONMENT

BEGIN_FOCUS
  Ship Probe
END_FOCUS

BEGIN_CAMERA
  TARGET Probe
  MODE Cockpit
  FOV 60.00
END_CAMERA

BEGIN_HUD
  TYPE Surface
END_HUD

BEGIN_SHIPS
Probe:AtmoProbe
  STATUS Landed Jupiter
  POS 0.0000000 -15.0000000
  HEADING 0.00
  TOUR 1500 470 8.0
  DRIFT 0.3
  SUNELEV 35
  CLOUDS 0
END
END_SHIPS
